  &lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; The proposed front porch, given its design, scale and
  fenestration details, would detract from the Arts and Crafts character of the
  host property and that of properties within the South Hill Conservation Area.
  The proposal would therefore result in an unduly obtrusive and incongruous
  addition to the original dwellinghouse, failing&amp;nbsp;to respect the character
  and proportions of the dwellinghouse and the visual amenities of the
  conservation area. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the high-quality
  design aspiration of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies
  D1, D3, D4 of The London Plan (2021), Policy GR1, SP2 and HE1 of the Harrow’s Local Plan
  (2021-2041), South Hill Conservation Area Study (2008) and the relevant
  provisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning Document Residential
  Design Guide (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
